g pressure  after applying each nail I'm curing all  of them for 90 seconds I'm gonna finish  it off with a thin layer of gel top coat  and cure that for 90 seconds I feel like  I never know how much glue is the right  amount of glue like I just keep adding  too much but then when I don't add too  much I add too little and the nail just  comes off  you definitely have to do this process  more than once I feel like to get  comfortable with all the products and  steps that you have to go through but  once you do get it I think the nails  feel really good it's been almost two  weeks and these press-ons are still  going strong I cannot believe I've never  tried this hack before it's so good  again it does take longer than just  using regular nail glue but I think it's  so worth it to use the gel glue the last  hack is using food coloring to create a  DIY lip stain so you basically make this  beautiful long lasting stain for just a  few bucks and you can technically mix up  whatever color you want I just realized  that I accidentally bought the powder  version of food coloring and not the  little liquidy Drip Drop kind I think it  should still work exactly the same I  just have to check the measurements I  want to make something  pinky like leaning towards pink maybe a  little orange something in that area so  I'm going to add some water now to make  it a liquidy consistency ooh is that  is that what it's gonna look like on my  lips  it feels like nothing is going off  and it looks way more pigmented the more  I layered it so now it does look like  I'm wearing lipstick it doesn't look as  natural but I'm gonna try to wipe off  the excess and see if it looks a little  better once this sets for a second I  definitely like it a lot better now that  I rubbed some of the bright pink away it  looks a lot more natural and subtle it's  nice to know though that with this hack  you can kind of build your own  pigmentation if you want a brighter  color just add more if you want a more  subtle color just rub some away and it  works really really nicely I definitely  would add gloss on top of this I think  I'm going to but I just wanted to see  no transfer  so I'm going to wear this for the rest  of the day and then check in with you  guys later to show you how the color has  held up the stain has definitely faded  but I can still see it which is good my  lips feel a bit drier than normal which  I don't love but I feel like the food  coloring is a pretty good option if you  want a long lasting lip stain  [Music]
 

